# Code owners.
#
# One owner for everything, deliberately. There is one committer today, and a
# file that lists people who do not exist yet is a file nobody updates when they
# do.
#
# This is a routing rule, not a permission. On its own it asks GitHub to request
# a review from the owner on any pull request touching a matching path; nothing
# stops a merge without that review until a ruleset requires it. This repository
# is public, so rulesets are available — see SECURITY.md for what to turn on.
#
# Order matters: the last matching pattern wins, so anything more specific
# belongs below the catch-all, not above it.

